Package: yume
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5.0),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Recommends:
 yume-daemon (= ${binary:Version})
Suggests:
 tor,
 yume-gui
Description: authenticated stealth transport command-line client
 YUME 0.3 development builds retain the reviewed transport-v2 runtime while
 the modular YTP/1 replacement is developed separately. The command-line
 client provides SOCKS, forwarding, packet, and service-stream modes.
 .
 This Debian build links against the system-installed libbasefwx for the
 cryptographic primitives used by mandatory composite authentication,
 ML-KEM-1024 + X25519 + PSK establishment, and the directional AEAD ratchet.

Package: yume-daemon
Architecture: any
Depends:
 libssl3t64 (>= 3.5.0),
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends}
Suggests:
 ssl-cert
Description: authenticated stealth transport server daemon
 YUME 0.3 development builds retain the reviewed transport-v2 runtime while
 the modular YTP/1 replacement is developed separately. Ordinary HTTP traffic
 is served through the configured cover path.
 .
 This package contains the yumed server daemon, a disabled-by-default
 systemd service, a locked service user, and the default /etc/yume
 configuration directory. It does not start listening on install; operators
 must first generate or provide TLS, authentication, and admission material.

Package: yume-gui
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!nogui>
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 yume (= ${binary:Version})
Recommends:
 libayatana-appindicator3-1
Description: graphical desktop client for the YUME transport
 yume-gui is the optional existing desktop consumer of the current
 transport-v2 facade. It provides client/server lifecycle, key management,
 relay tools, status, logs, and system-tray integration.
 .
 The GUI remains available during the modular transition; it is not evidence
 that the experimental role-neutral ABI or YTP/1 provider is complete.
